From: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as21xxx: report multi-gigabit link partner abilities

as21xxx_read_status() only decodes the link partner advertisement from the
C22 registers mapped into the AN MMD, which stop at 1000BASE-T. On a link
negotiated at 2.5G ethtool therefore reports:

  Link partner advertised link modes: 10baseT/Half 10baseT/Full
                                      100baseT/Half 100baseT/Full
                                      1000baseT/Full
  Speed: 2500Mb/s

The multi-gigabit abilities are available in the C45 10GBASE-T AN status
register (7.33), which reads 0xd5e1 in the case above: LP2_5G and LP5G set,
LP10G clear, exactly matching the link partner. LOCOK however stays clear,
as the firmware drives autonegotiation on its own and does not maintain the
standard AN bookkeeping. The 10GBASE-T AN control register (7.32) shows the
same, it reads back without any of the ADV2_5G, ADV5G or ADV10G bits even
though those speeds are advertised.

OpenWrt's pending patch 713 changes
mii_10gbt_stat_mod_linkmode_lpa_t() to discard the whole word unless both
LOCOK and REMOK are set. Decode the three ability bits directly to avoid
that OpenWrt-specific gating. Clear them together with the C22 ones while
autonegotiation is still running.

Signed-off-by: Pietro Ameruoso <p.ameruoso@live.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as21xxx.c
@@ -781,6 +781,34 @@ static int as21xxx_read_c22_lpa(struct p
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* The mapped C22 registers stop at 1000BASE-T, the multi-gigabit abilities of
+ * the link partner are only reported in the C45 10GBASE-T AN status register.
+ * The firmware runs autonegotiation on its own and leaves LOCOK clear there,
+ * so decode the ability bits directly instead of using
+ * mii_10gbt_stat_mod_linkmode_lpa_t(), which under OpenWrt's pending patch
+ * 713 discards the whole word unless both LOCOK and REMOK are set.
+ */
+static int as21xxx_read_ng_lpa(struct phy_device *phydev)
+{
+	int lpa;
+
+	lpa = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_AN, MDIO_AN_10GBT_STAT);
+	if (lpa < 0)
+		return lpa;
+
+	linkmode_mod_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_2500baseT_Full_BIT,
+			 phydev->lp_advertising,
+			 lpa & MDIO_AN_10GBT_STAT_LP2_5G);
+	linkmode_mod_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_5000baseT_Full_BIT,
+			 phydev->lp_advertising,
+			 lpa & MDIO_AN_10GBT_STAT_LP5G);
+	linkmode_mod_bit(ETHTOOL_LINK_MODE_10000baseT_Full_BIT,
+			 phydev->lp_advertising,
+			 lpa & MDIO_AN_10GBT_STAT_LP10G);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int as21xxx_read_status(struct phy_device *phydev)
 {
 	int bmcr, old_link = phydev->link;
@@ -805,12 +833,18 @@ static int as21xxx_read_status(struct ph
 			mii_stat1000_mod_linkmode_lpa_t(phydev->lp_advertising,
 							0);
 			mii_lpa_mod_linkmode_lpa_t(phydev->lp_advertising, 0);
+			mii_10gbt_stat_mod_linkmode_lpa_t(phydev->lp_advertising,
+							  0);
 			return 0;
 		}
 
 		ret = as21xxx_read_c22_lpa(phydev);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
+
+		ret = as21xxx_read_ng_lpa(phydev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
 	} else {
 		linkmode_zero(phydev->lp_advertising);
 	}
